:"brown","kme":0.573281,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.552322,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000196531","module":"brown","kme":0.484196,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.852428,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_id":"ENSG00000196531","module":"red","kme":0.53174,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.398013,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000196531","module":"turquoise","kme":0.170225,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000196531","module":"turquoise","kme":0.175079,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000196531","entrez_id":["4666"],"uniprot":["E9PAV3","Q13765"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a protein that associates with basic transcription factor 3 (BTF3) to form the nascent polypeptide-associated complex (NAC). This complex binds to nascent proteins that lack a signal peptide motif as they emerge from the ribosome, blocking interaction with the signal recognition particle (SRP) and preventing mistranslocation to the endoplasmic reticulum. This protein is an IgE autoantigen in atopic dermatitis patients. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants, but the full length nature of some of these variants, including those encoding very large proteins, has not been determined. There are multiple pseudogenes of this gene on different chromosomes. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"E9PAV3","text":"Cardiac- and muscle-specific transcription factor. May act to regulate the expression of genes involved in the development of myotubes. Plays a critical role in ventricular cardiomyocyte expansion and regulates postnatal skeletal muscle growth and regeneration. Involved in the organized assembly of thick and thin filaments of myofibril sarcomeres (By similarity)."},{"accession":"Q13765","text":"Prevents inappropriate targeting of non-secretory polypeptides to the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). Binds to nascent polypeptide chains as they emerge from the ribosome and blocks their interaction with the signal recognition particle (SRP), which normally targets nascent secretory peptides to the ER. Also reduces the inherent affinity of ribosomes for protein translocation sites in the ER membrane (M sites). May act as a specific coactivator for JUN, binding to DNA and stabilizing the interaction of JUN homodimers with target gene promoters."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}